       transition: transform 180ms ease, background 180ms ease;
     }

     .question[aria-expanded="true"] .icon {
       transform: rotate(45deg);
       background: rgba(142, 162, 255, 0.18);
     }

     .details {
       padding: 0 22px 22px;
       color: var(--muted);
       line-height: 1.7;
     }

     .details[hidden] {
       display: none;
     }

     .details p {
       margin: 0;
     }

     @media (max-width: 640px) {
       .page {
         padding: 22px 16px;
         border-radius: 20px;
       }

       .question,
       .details {
         padding-left: 16px;
         padding-right: 16px;
       }
     }
   </style>
 </head>
 <body>
   <main class="page">
     <p class="eyebrow">Cat FAQ</p>
     <h1>Common questions about cats</h1>
     <p class="intro">
       Learn about feline behavior, care, and quirky habits with this compact FAQ. All answers are
       collapsed by default, so you can open only the ones you want to read.
     </p>

     <section class="faq" aria-label="Frequently asked questions about cats">
       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="details-1">
           <span>Why do cats purr?</span>
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="details-1" hidden>
           <p>
             Cats often purr when they feel relaxed and content, but they may also purr when they
             want comfort, attention, or reassurance. It can be a soothing behavior in both happy
             and stressful situations.
           </p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="details-2">
           <span>Why do cats knead blankets and laps?</span>
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="details-2" hidden>
           <p>
             Kneading is a behavior kittens use while nursing, and many adult cats keep doing it
             because it feels comforting. It can also be a way for them to mark a favorite spot with
             scent glands in their paws.
           </p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="details-3">
           <span>How much sleep do cats need?</span>
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="details-3" hidden>
           <p>
             Most cats sleep for around 12 to 16 hours a day, and some sleep even more. Their
             natural rhythm includes bursts of energy followed by long periods of rest, especially if
             they are young, older, or mostly indoors.
           </p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="details-4">
           <span>Why do cats bring “gifts” like toys or prey?</span>
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="details-4" hidden>
           <p>
             This behavior is tied to instinct. A cat may be practicing hunting skills, showing off
             a successful catch, or treating you like part of its family by sharing something it
             considers valuable.
           </p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="details-5">
           <span>What helps keep an indoor cat happy?</span>
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="details-5" hidden>
           <p>
             Indoor cats do best with play, climbing spots, scratching surfaces, hiding places, and
             regular interaction. Rotating toys and offering window views can also help prevent
             boredom and support healthy behavior.
           </p>
         </div>
       </div>
     </section>
   </main>

   <script>
     const questions = document.querySelectorAll(".question");

     questions.forEach((button) => {
       button.addEventListener("click", () => {
         const detailsId = button.getAttribute("aria-controls");
         const details = document.getElementById(detailsId);
         const isExpanded = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";

         button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isExpanded));
         details.hidden = isExpanded;
       });
     });
   </script>
 </body>
 </html>

